# The preset shape table is embedded with `include_str!` and its loader verifies
# an FNV-1a checksum of the exact body bytes. A CRLF checkout (Windows with
# `core.autocrlf`) changes those bytes, the table is refused, and every preset
# shape paints as its bounding rectangle. Keep it LF on every platform.
crates/casual-doc-model/data/preset_shapes.txt text eol=lf

# Generated from the capability registry and compared byte for byte by
# `crates/casual-doc-command/tests/generated.rs` and `opendoc-command-gen --check`
# (`docs/181` G4). A CRLF checkout made every file "stale" on Windows.
webapp/generated/** text eol=lf

# A PDF is binary whatever its bytes look like: its cross-reference table holds
# byte offsets, so a CRLF checkout breaks every file Git mistakes for text (a small,
# NUL-free hand-written fixture is exactly that), and Windows CI read the encrypted
# fixture as "not a readable PDF" (PR #899).
*.pdf binary
# Compared against a fresh measurement run (docs/182 P0).
fixtures/pdf/measurement.json text eol=lf
